{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/922403-black-market-exigence","id":922403,"title":"Black Market Exigence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-27T20:25:13-07:00","id":922403,"title":"Black Market Exigence","content":"So Let's say the god of the Ruby Library Upon the Tomb of the House of Yeld decides it needs an exalted champion, instead of doing things through proper channels Ruby calls in a few favors and lands herself an exigence that was slated for Hanuk the god of Ice and Bones in a valley way to the north. <br /> <br /> Who is diminished/killed when the exigence is fused to the mortal? Who decided how much power to invest? and whose themes are carried along into the exalt's charmset/anima powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T20:32:18-07:00","id":922410,"title":"","content":"We don't know yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T20:41:43-07:00","id":922421,"title":"","content":"Extrapolating from the Janest fiction and dev comments, it seems to me that Exigence is a &quot;last-minute&quot; thing. The god who &quot;uses&quot; it is the god that gets diminished, as it takes of their essence when it's &quot;applied&quot; and seemingly not before (or if so then it doesn't seem to affect the god until it's applied, holding the essence in a sort of metaphysical escrow).<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how &quot;dirty bombs&quot; fit into this, nor how the gods that muck around with Exigence before its final delivery benefit from it (outside of giving a big &quot;fuck you&quot; to their rival). Would they get their essence burned away too? Maybe it's a way for them to &quot;share the load&quot;? idunno.<br /> <br /> Edit : although, admittedly, if the only god to be diminished is the one that filed the petition, it adds a level of interest and intrigue as stealing it is suddenly a LOT more worth it. I'd probably go with that for the time being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 06-27-2016, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T21:32:27-07:00","id":922453,"title":"","content":"By my reading, the &quot;divine fire&quot; of the Exigence is catalyzed by the god paying the price to become the Exaltation (&quot;An Exigent will be the Chosen of the god who catalyzes the Unconquered Sun\u2019s divine power... &quot; ; &quot;Before being catalyzed into Exaltation, the divine power of the Unconquered Sun may be stolen or traded, perhaps even falling into the hands of criminal or forbidden gods.&quot; p52). As such, Ruby Library Upon the Tomb of the House of Yeld would not have the Exaltation--they would simply have the divine fire of Exigence. To turn that fire into a true Exaltation, the price must still be paid--and whoever pays that price determines (by the facets of the essence spent) the powers of that Exaltation.<br /> <br /> Whether or not they <b><i>also</i></b> choose the recipient is unclear. Perhaps they work in pairs if too weak; one black-market god pays the price to catalyze, and the other gives the Exaltation to their Chosen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":11797,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","user":"Seeker","date":".  I KEEP EDITING AAAH 06-28-2016, 12:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T23:55:00-07:00","id":922486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/922403-black-market-exigence?p=922453#post922453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether or not they <b><i>also</i></b> choose the recipient is unclear. Perhaps they work in pairs if too weak; one black-market god pays the price to catalyze, and the other gives the Exaltation to their Chosen.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me think of a particularly evil god i have been thinking.... One in Nexus. Trades in the Divine Fire for those desperate in getting them but... Eats the gods that are weakened by them.. Uses their essence to strengthen themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T04:33:36-07:00","id":922540,"title":"","content":"I'd say it's definitely the god who activates the Exaltation (or divine fire, if you prefer) that pays the cost. Otherwise it's pretty much the highest form of currency, as well as a final, bold play for most gods. Powerful and deserving gods sell their Exaltation to other gods in return for a tithe or other favours (probably the other favours, given that minor gods are likely to combust if they use the thing), while small gods sell bigger gods their gifted Exaltations for power or perhaps additional spheres of influence currently under the purview of that god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T06:14:05-07:00","id":922570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Not Quite Simple Soul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/922403-black-market-exigence#post922403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Let's say the god of the Ruby Library Upon the Tomb of the House of Yeld decides it needs an exalted champion, instead of doing things through proper channels Ruby calls in a few favors and lands herself an exigence that was slated for Hanuk the god of Ice and Bones in a valley way to the north.<br /> <br /> Who is diminished/killed when the exigence is fused to the mortal? Who decided how much power to invest? and whose themes are carried along into the exalt's charmset/anima powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Which one is a better story for your PCs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}